# Client UI components (required)

Read `AGENTS.md` for full instructions.

## Reuse before creating

Check `client/src/components/ui/` first. Reuse `Button`, `Input`, `PasswordInput`, `FormField`, `FormActions`, `Modal`, `FormModal`, `Table`, `Dropdown`, and `Spinner`. Create a new file in that folder only when no existing component fits.

## Loading states

- `Button`: always pass `loading` + `loadingText` during async actions
- `Table`: use `loading` prop for list fetch states
- Never show a clickable submit button without a spinner while saving

## Save button activation

| Form type | Submit enabled when |
|-----------|---------------------|
| **Create** | All required fields filled (`areRequiredFieldsFilled`) |
| **Edit** | At least one field changed vs original (`hasFormChanges`) |

Use `submitDisabled` on `FormActions` / `FormModal`, or `disabled` on `Button`.

Helpers live in `client/src/utils/form.ts`: `areRequiredFieldsFilled`, `hasFormChanges`, `pickChangedFields`.

## Partial updates (DB)

- **Client:** PATCH/send only changed fields via `pickChangedFields`
- **Server:** Apply only fields present in the request body

## Password inputs

Use `PasswordInput` (show/hide toggle). Do not use raw `Input type="password"`.

## Icons

Use `react-icons` with colorful Tailwind classes on buttons, dropdown items, and actions.
